TIME(3)                        P32W Unix                         TIME(3)

NAME
       time, ctime, localtime, gmtime, asctime - convert times to dates

SYNOPSIS
       #include <time.h>

       time_t time(time_t *t);
       char *ctime(const time_t *t);
       struct tm *localtime(const time_t *t);
       struct tm *gmtime(const time_t *t);
       char *asctime(const struct tm *tm);

       struct tm {
           int tm_sec;     /* seconds, 0-59 */
           int tm_min;     /* minutes, 0-59 */
           int tm_hour;    /* hours, 0-23 */
           int tm_mday;    /* day of the month, 1-31 */
           int tm_mon;     /* month, 0-11: January is 0 */
           int tm_year;    /* year - 1900 */
           int tm_wday;    /* day of the week, 0-6: Sunday is 0 */
           int tm_yday;    /* day of the year, 0-365 */
           int tm_isdst;   /* 1 in summer time, else 0 */
       };

DESCRIPTION
       The kernel counts time as a time_t: the seconds since
       00:00:00 UTC on 1 January 1970. time(2), a system call,
       returns the current one. The functions here turn it into a
       date.

       gmtime breaks the time *t down into a struct tm in UTC.
       localtime does the same in local time: the time zone, and
       its rule for summer time, come from TZ (see tzset(3); without
       TZ or /etc/TZ local time is UTC); tm_isdst says whether
       summer time was in force.

       asctime writes the date tm as a string of 25 characters in
       the form of V7's ctime, ended by a newline and a NUL:

           Thu Oct 14 12:30:00 2026\n

       (a day of the month below 10 has a space for its tens).
       ctime(t) is asctime(localtime(t)).

       The zone's name is tzname[tm.tm_isdst] (tzset(3)).

RETURN VALUE
       Pointers to static storage: one struct tm shared by gmtime,
       localtime (and so ctime and mktime(3)), and one string shared
       by asctime and ctime. Each call overwrites the last; copy
       what must be kept.

EXAMPLES
       time_t now = time(0);
       struct tm *tm = localtime(&now);
       printf("%02d:%02d %s\n", tm->tm_hour, tm->tm_min,
              tzname[tm->tm_isdst]);
       fputs(ctime(&now), stdout);

SEE ALSO
       date(1), time(2), mktime(3), tzset(3), tz(5)

BUGS
       time_t is a 32-bit int: the count runs out in January 2038,
       and times before 1970 (negative) come out wrong. There is no
       strftime, difftime, clock, or reentrant form (localtime_r);
       struct tm has no tm_gmtoff or tm_zone.
